course: dictionary
lesson: 1715
title: Circuits
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A circuit is a loop. Electricity can only flow when it has a complete loop to go round, from the battery, through the bulb and back again. «Electricity only flows when it has a complete loop to go round, from the battery, through the bulb and back again; that loop is called a circuit.» So the word means the whole loop, not just one wire.
explain: Look at the clues in «A battery stores energy in chemicals and pushes electricity round the circuit until the chemicals are used up.» The battery pushes the electricity, and the circuit is the route it travels. Round means around, so the circuit goes round in a loop.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Electricity flows only around a complete loop» still makes sense, so circuit means a loop that electricity goes around. When your meaning fits every time, you have probably found it.
fact: A circuit is a complete loop of wires and parts that electricity flows round.
fact: A circuit must be complete for electricity to flow; if the loop is broken, it is an open circuit and the electricity stops.
fact: A battery pushes electricity round the circuit until its chemicals are used up.
fact: A circuit can also be a route that goes round in a loop, like a racing circuit, and one trip round that loop is also a circuit.
fact: Circuit training in PE is exercise where you go round a set of different activities.
exercise: «Electricity flows only around a complete circuit.» What is a circuit? | *A complete loop of wires and parts that electricity flows round | A switch that is always off | A single long wire with no ends | A kind of battery
exercise: In PE, the teacher says, «Let's do a circuit: ten jumps, ten squats, then rest, and repeat.» What is a circuit here? | *A set of different exercises done round in a loop | Ten squats only | A kind of jumping rope | A racing car that drives fast
exercise: «A switch opens or closes the circuit.» What does the switch do to the circuit? | It turns the bulb into a buzzer | It makes the battery bigger | *It opens or closes it, so electricity can stop or flow | It makes the circuit longer
test: «A series circuit has only one path for electricity.» What does a series circuit have? | A broken bulb | Many paths and no loop | No battery at all | *One path for electricity to go round
test: Why must a circuit be complete for a bulb to light? | So the battery can rest | So the bulb can become bigger | So the wires can get hot and stop | *So electricity has a full loop to flow round
exam: «The fuse box has circuit breakers that switch off a circuit when too much current flows.» What does circuit mean here? | *A loop of wires that electricity flows round | A trip round a track | A racing track for cars | A kind of exercise
